-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:f764b056896ab4d05f9f548ab49493ee7bbae8f4ba5d7e813aaf2855f01bab60","file":"preprints/Thomason-Model-Structures-in-Every-Strict-Higher-Dimension-September-25-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":41,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"1caab4a218e58a7da193ca669054a97bfb38cf1692885a49abd2053d39a233cc","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Thomason-Model-Structures-in-Every-Strict-Higher-Dimension-September-25-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:f764b056896ab4d05f9f548ab49493ee7bbae8f4ba5d7e813aaf2855f01bab60","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Thomason-Model-Structures-in-Every-Strict-Higher-Dimension-September-25-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L41"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nFor every $n\\in\\{1,2,3,\\ldots\\}\\cup\\{\\infty\\}$, the classes\n$(C_n,W_n,F_n)$ in \\eqref{eq:prescribed-classes} form a proper\ncombinatorial model structure on $\\nCat$. It is cofibrantly generated by\n$(L_nI,L_nJ)$, where\n\\[\n I=\\{\\partial\\Delta[m]\\hookrightarrow\\Delta[m]:m\\ge0\\},\\qquad\n J=\\{\\Lambda^k[m]\\hookrightarrow\\Delta[m]:m\\ge1,\\ 0\\le k\\le m\\}.\n\\]\nMoreover,\n\\[\n L_n:\\sSet_{\\KQ}\\rightleftarrows(\\nCat,C_n,W_n,F_n):R_n\n\\]\nis a Quillen equivalence."}
